1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:01,330
Hey.

2
00:00:01,610 --> 00:00:03,540
Welcome back to Steadfast Men.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,530
This is Lesson Twelve.

4
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:08,740
It's called A Man with No Brothers.

5
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:10,950
Here's how this goes.

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,410
The quiet after you lock up.

7
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:17,180
A brother beside you, and a man ahead of you.

8
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:21,130
What happened, what's heavy, what's next.

9
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,510
Hollis, and a man who notices.

10
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:28,500
The question you bring, and the yes you can give.

11
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:32,000
A name, or the honesty of no name.

12
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,980
Last lesson was When Home Never Handed You Off.

13
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,999
You were asked to put a date in your Bible,

14
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:43,090
and then tell one brother where you stood with the door,

15
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,930
and name the day if the knock was safe.

16
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:47,780
Maybe you wrote the date.

17
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:50,070
Maybe the line is still blank.

18
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:52,490
That house never said go.

19
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:55,780
You can walk out without making the door a weapon.

20
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:58,900
The man you can call is another matter.

21
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:00,740
New to this?

22
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:03,710
Hold to one lesson at a time.

23
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:06,240
This lesson is the one to begin.

24
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:08,400
Lessons before it can wait.

25
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:10,590
I'm Wes.

26
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:13,440
You can look steady from where I stand.

27
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:15,210
People know your name.

28
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:17,930
You answer when a need goes around.

29
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:20,090
Then the day ends.

30
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,360
You lock up.

31
00:01:21,810 --> 00:01:22,570
You sit a minute.

32
00:01:23,130 --> 00:01:26,320
And there's not a man you would call and tell the truth to.

33
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,470
I've lived right there.

34
00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:31,050
I called it a private life.

35
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,960
Private meant nobody was allowed in.

36
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:36,520
I called the quiet peace.

37
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,510
It was a shut door with a nice name on it.

38
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:45,180
Maybe you're young, and you figure this arrives later, when the life gets bigger.

39
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:46,520
It doesn't.

40
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:50,210
Or maybe you're married, and you figure your wife covers it.

41
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:51,610
She loves you.

42
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:56,000
She was never built to be the only one who knows when you're sinking.

43
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:58,440
Or maybe the work went well.

44
00:01:58,850 --> 00:02:00,070
The day looked clean.

45
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:02,920
You still couldn't say who has you.

46
00:02:04,030 --> 00:02:05,690
So here is the aim.

47
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,950
Name that aloneness.

48
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,070
Then make an ask.

49
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:11,490
You go first.

50
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:15,040
Nobody drafts you off a wall because you looked ready.

51
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:19,680
If you fell, the man you could call might still be a blank.

52
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,880
Look that blank in the face before you're done.

53
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:26,600
A name, or the honesty of no name.

54
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:31,850
One sentence puts four marks on a real man.

55
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,000
Here they are.

56
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:40,220
A steadfast man ends the wait, takes up what is his to carry, moves before he is called,

57
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:45,550
and receives God's pay, while a crowd's approval stays out of the wage.

58
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:51,410
I want them pointed at the man who has you, and at the man you haven't asked.

59
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:54,970
Passivity can look like patience.

60
00:02:55,370 --> 00:02:56,670
You wait to be chosen.

61
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,020
You call the waiting humility.

62
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:02,090
It's often just fear with a calm face.

63
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:07,510
A man can hit his numbers and still be passive where it actually counts.

64
00:03:08,030 --> 00:03:10,930
Nobody at the job is going to ask him if he has a brother.

65
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:13,030
That question is his.

66
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,560
The ask doesn't wait on a mood.

67
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:19,500
The mood shows up later, after the sentence is already out.

68
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,500
So you say it scared.

69
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,900
The ask belongs to you.

70
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,190
Accept that.

71
00:03:25,570 --> 00:03:26,580
Set the time.

72
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,090
Say the sentence.

73
00:03:28,470 --> 00:03:31,040
That's responsibility with a phone in your hand.

74
00:03:32,270 --> 00:03:34,780
Courage sounds smaller than men think.

75
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:38,620
Courage is saying the awkward thing before you feel ready.

76
00:03:39,210 --> 00:03:42,560
And God's pay is a life God can actually help.

77
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,420
Privacy can feel like a prize.

78
00:03:45,910 --> 00:03:48,400
Privacy pays you in being untouched.

79
00:03:48,910 --> 00:03:53,450
God's pay is a man who can be helped, and who can turn around and help.

80
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:57,540
If you fell, somebody's name ought to be ready.

81
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:01,400
And somewhere near you is a man about twenty years ahead,

82
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,970
living a stretch you've never asked him about.

83
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:07,610
Both of those silences are the same passivity.

84
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:10,970
You don't outgrow those silences by getting busier.

85
00:04:11,370 --> 00:04:13,490
You break them by going first.

86
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:17,750
Ecclesiastes four, verse ten.

87
00:04:18,390 --> 00:04:21,750
"If either of them falls down, one can help the other up.

88
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:26,130
But pity anyone who falls and has no one to help them up."

89
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:30,280
Strength was never the promise that you wouldn't fall.

90
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:34,390
The promise in the verse is a hand close enough to get under you.

91
00:04:35,030 --> 00:04:38,410
Pity, in this verse, is a warning with mercy in it.

92
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:42,030
You can have a full calendar and still be that man.

93
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,650
People like you.

94
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:45,050
They count on you.

95
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:48,250
None of that is a hand on the day you go down.

96
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:52,020
Falling doesn't always look like a scene.

97
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:55,010
Sometimes falling is a slow slide.

98
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:56,280
The temper.

99
00:04:56,930 --> 00:04:57,530
The secret.

100
00:04:58,310 --> 00:04:59,730
The distance at the table.

101
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:02,460
Most men don't announce the slide.

102
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,830
Those men just get harder to find.

103
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:09,900
A hand can still reach that slide, if a man is close enough to notice.

104
00:05:11,010 --> 00:05:13,180
Proverbs thirteen, verse twenty.

105
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:19,150
"Walk with the wise and become wise, for a companion of fools suffers harm."

106
00:05:20,550 --> 00:05:23,990
So the man you tie yourself to is going to leave a mark.

107
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:27,950
Walk with a wise man and his counsel gets into your feet.

108
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:33,910
Walk with a man who only nods, and you will go farther down a bad road feeling supported.

109
00:05:35,130 --> 00:05:36,940
You can have plenty of agreement.

110
00:05:37,350 --> 00:05:42,260
What you're short on is a man who loves you enough to disagree and then stay.

111
00:05:42,810 --> 00:05:44,570
That man is the brother.

112
00:05:45,050 --> 00:05:46,770
Christ stays the Savior.

113
00:05:47,210 --> 00:05:49,000
The Father stays the Father.

114
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:54,540
A brother stands with you on a day you can't find God, until you can hear Him again.

115
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,300
One man like that.

116
00:05:56,910 --> 00:05:58,730
Two, if God is kind.

117
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:01,800
You don't need a crowd to stop living unknown.

118
00:06:03,670 --> 00:06:05,650
A buddy is a good thing.

119
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:11,870
A buddy is the man beside you while something gets done, or while something gets enjoyed.

120
00:06:12,550 --> 00:06:13,770
You split a lunch.

121
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,110
You loan a ladder.

122
00:06:15,630 --> 00:06:18,190
You both show up when a family needs a hand.

123
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,910
Keep those men.

124
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:21,710
Thank God for them.

125
00:06:22,850 --> 00:06:25,050
A brother is a different seat.

126
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:28,670
A brother knows what you do when a day goes sour.

127
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:33,480
Whether you pick a fight, or you go polish a thing that was already fine,

128
00:06:34,010 --> 00:06:37,280
or you get real helpful and real gone.

129
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,910
A brother can ask about the money.

130
00:06:40,390 --> 00:06:42,090
About the way you spoke at home.

131
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:43,700
About the late hour.

132
00:06:44,230 --> 00:06:47,510
About whether you prayed, or just performed a prayer.

133
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:48,840
And you tell him.

134
00:06:49,470 --> 00:06:54,530
He says the hard sentence once, with love, and he doesn't sand it down.

135
00:06:55,090 --> 00:06:58,580
Then he shows up the next time like the sentence didn't end you.

136
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,620
I've been very known on the subject of sauce.

137
00:07:03,070 --> 00:07:05,630
My text thread can settle the sauce.

138
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,660
The thread can't settle me.

139
00:07:08,310 --> 00:07:11,760
I'd come in the door, set my keys down the same way,

140
00:07:12,010 --> 00:07:15,130
and my wife could read the whole day off that sound.

141
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:17,630
I called it being easy.

142
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,170
Low maintenance.

143
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:25,320
What it was, my wife was carrying the weight of being the only person who knew me.

144
00:07:25,970 --> 00:07:27,550
She is a gift.

145
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:31,340
That weight was never supposed to be her whole assignment.

146
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:35,550
If you went down, is a man's name ready?

147
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:38,680
Your wife doesn't fill this blank.

148
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:43,690
The men at your work can respect you and never hear what you're afraid of.

149
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:46,510
A good crew is still a gift.

150
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:50,220
You need one man who is allowed all the way in.

151
00:07:52,150 --> 00:07:54,080
Here is what a man tells himself.

152
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,320
He says he is fine.

153
00:07:56,960 --> 00:08:00,170
I've said it with a straight face on days I wasn't fine.

154
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:03,540
Fine is pride that learned manners.

155
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,590
A man says there's no time.

156
00:08:07,250 --> 00:08:07,990
There's time.

157
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:13,010
What there hasn't been is an ask small enough to fit inside a real life.

158
00:08:14,110 --> 00:08:16,630
A man says he doesn't want to be a weight.

159
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:21,660
Under that, you may have learned early that needing somebody cost extra.

160
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:24,600
So you would rather go under than reach.

161
00:08:25,670 --> 00:08:28,070
A man says men don't do this.

162
00:08:28,470 --> 00:08:32,930
Men did this long before a sealed-up life was treated as the mature one.

163
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,850
Or maybe you tried.

164
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:39,350
You opened your chest and a man used what he heard.

165
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,470
I'm not going to shrink that.

166
00:08:41,970 --> 00:08:43,370
That wound is real.

167
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:45,960
The wound can still try to run you.

168
00:08:46,350 --> 00:08:50,470
One man who failed you doesn't get to lock the rest of your years.

169
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:57,790
There was a man at our church, older than me, always by the coat rack once people had gone.

170
00:08:58,550 --> 00:08:59,780
I had questions.

171
00:09:00,470 --> 00:09:03,640
How a house stays kind when the money gets thin.

172
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:07,270
I walked past that man for a long time.

173
00:09:07,850 --> 00:09:09,610
I told myself he looked busy.

174
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:12,390
He was putting an arm through a sleeve.

175
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:16,870
That's a man with half a minute and nowhere he had to be yet.

176
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:20,870
I had that man cast as too important to bother.

177
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,840
He was waiting on a jacket.

178
00:09:23,510 --> 00:09:26,450
The fear dressed itself up as respect.

179
00:09:27,070 --> 00:09:27,820
I nodded.

180
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:28,990
I left.

181
00:09:29,670 --> 00:09:31,730
I still think about that sleeve.

182
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:35,050
I walked by as if that man were scenery.

183
00:09:35,750 --> 00:09:36,910
He might have said no.

184
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,990
I never gave him the chance.

185
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:43,940
A no would've been cleaner than another stretch of guessing on my own.

186
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:48,450
Most men I know already want a brother.

187
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:54,550
What those men don't have is a picture small enough to survive the life they live.

188
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:57,710
The pictures handed to them are huge.

189
00:09:58,330 --> 00:10:02,780
A man with a baby in the house, or a stretch where the work is eating him,

190
00:10:03,150 --> 00:10:05,730
looks at those pictures and does nothing.

191
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,680
So take a smaller picture.

192
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:09,990
One man.

193
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,280
One table.

194
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:13,390
One honest question.

195
00:10:13,950 --> 00:10:15,730
Kept, not crammed.

196
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,520
A plan that floats is a plan that dies.

197
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:24,910
Pick a man you can tell the whole truth, with no paycheck between you.

198
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:26,370
What happened.

199
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:27,590
Not a report.

200
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,020
What's heavy.

201
00:10:29,570 --> 00:10:31,560
This is the one that earns the time.

202
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:33,300
Name the load.

203
00:10:33,690 --> 00:10:35,100
Name the fear under it.

204
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:37,240
Both of you tell the truth.

205
00:10:37,730 --> 00:10:39,880
The man listening has one job.

206
00:10:40,330 --> 00:10:41,260
He listens.

207
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:42,740
Fixing can wait.

208
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,230
What's next.

209
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:49,490
Name one move before you leave the table, out loud, so a man heard it.

210
00:10:50,010 --> 00:10:53,590
When you sit back down, you start with whether the move got done.

211
00:10:54,130 --> 00:10:55,420
Leave room at the end.

212
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:57,150
Pray out loud.

213
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:58,610
You for him.

214
00:10:58,900 --> 00:10:59,760
Him for you.

215
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:04,890
Some days one of the two is a wreck, and the heavy thing takes the whole talk.

216
00:11:05,310 --> 00:11:06,770
That's what the time is for.

217
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,590
The floor doesn't move.

218
00:11:09,190 --> 00:11:12,324
Without those questions, two men will talk weather

219
00:11:12,324 --> 00:11:15,000
until the clock dies and nobody was known.

220
00:11:15,450 --> 00:11:17,010
I learned that by failing it.

221
00:11:17,530 --> 00:11:19,802
A man started telling me what was heavy,

222
00:11:19,802 --> 00:11:23,230
and I handed him three ideas before he finished the sentence.

223
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,540
He went quiet.

224
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:27,090
I said, I just did the thing.

225
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,770
You don't need a plan from me.

226
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:29,810
I'm here.

227
00:11:30,330 --> 00:11:32,980
I almost ruined the talk by being helpful.

228
00:11:33,530 --> 00:11:34,400
Help can wait.

229
00:11:34,910 --> 00:11:36,710
A brother stays in the chair.

230
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:40,080
I'll call him Hollis.

231
00:11:40,690 --> 00:11:44,440
Hollis ran the meal list when a family hit a hard stretch.

232
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:48,590
Hollis showed up in other men's trouble like it was his trade.

233
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:52,370
What Hollis didn't have was a man in his own.

234
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:58,630
At home there was a boy who had started shutting a door harder than the door deserved.

235
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:04,060
Hollis would stand in the hall, hand on the frame, and come up empty.

236
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:06,970
His wife said one sentence.

237
00:12:07,450 --> 00:12:08,180
Not loud.

238
00:12:08,890 --> 00:12:12,610
I'm tired of being the only one who knows when you're not alright.

239
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:16,300
Hollis nodded, like she had mentioned the weather.

240
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:17,940
She didn't smile.

241
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:21,900
Hollis sat on that sentence for months.

242
00:12:22,510 --> 00:12:27,980
Hollis told me later he lined up men in his head and talked himself out of each one.

243
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:29,650
There was a neighbor.

244
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:33,560
Hollis didn't want the fence between their yards to get heavy.

245
00:12:34,570 --> 00:12:37,280
Then Hollis stayed late to put chairs up,

246
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:41,360
and a quieter man was still there, rinsing the coffee pot.

247
00:12:42,070 --> 00:12:44,020
The one who never worked a crowd.

248
00:12:44,790 --> 00:12:46,670
Hollis heard his own mouth.

249
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:51,000
I'm trying to be a better man, and I don't have a brother.

250
00:12:51,730 --> 00:12:57,810
Would you talk with me, one man to another, plain and honest, and see if it holds.

251
00:12:59,030 --> 00:13:01,080
The quieter man looked at the pot.

252
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:03,730
I water the garden most evenings.

253
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:05,150
Call while I do that.

254
00:13:05,650 --> 00:13:07,250
Don't build a program out of it.

255
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:12,500
The first few calls, Hollis reported on other people's suppers.

256
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:14,540
The quieter man let him.

257
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:21,270
One evening Hollis said, I'm short with my boy, and I don't know the next sentence.

258
00:13:21,830 --> 00:13:24,670
The quieter man didn't hand Hollis a speech.

259
00:13:25,170 --> 00:13:30,170
The quieter man said, say it again next time, and tell me if you caught it sooner.

260
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:33,870
Hollis told me what actually moved him.

261
00:13:34,470 --> 00:13:37,750
If Hollis didn't call, the quieter man noticed.

262
00:13:38,310 --> 00:13:41,290
Just one man, expecting Hollis.

263
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:42,970
That's a brother.

264
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:46,950
A brother knows the stretch you're in.

265
00:13:47,510 --> 00:13:50,240
You also need a man who has come out the other side.

266
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,490
About twenty years ahead of you.

267
00:13:52,950 --> 00:13:56,640
That man has already walked ground you're just entering.

268
00:13:57,790 --> 00:14:00,250
Maybe you're the younger man, and you wait.

269
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:05,530
You figure the older one is busy, or that a real man sorts his own mess,

270
00:14:05,910 --> 00:14:08,790
or that asking would admit your father never said it.

271
00:14:09,350 --> 00:14:12,500
Or maybe you're the older man, and you wait too.

272
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:18,590
You figure a young man doesn't want an old opinion, or that your mistakes disqualified you.

273
00:14:19,110 --> 00:14:20,840
So you wait each other out.

274
00:14:21,350 --> 00:14:25,250
Boys become men with nobody ahead telling them what's coming.

275
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:29,020
Second Timothy two, verse two.

276
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:34,785
"And the things you have heard me say in the presence of many witnesses

277
00:14:34,785 --> 00:14:39,160
entrust to reliable people who will also be qualified to teach others."

278
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,600
That chain doesn't mend itself.

279
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:45,120
Somebody has to open his mouth.

280
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:48,040
Don't lead with a big title.

281
00:14:48,710 --> 00:14:49,330
I did.

282
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:52,200
I used a word that sounded like a job.

283
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:57,430
The man I asked got a look like I'd handed him a uniform he hadn't agreed to wear.

284
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:01,370
I backpedaled so hard I nearly took the question with me.

285
00:15:02,030 --> 00:15:04,610
What I meant was one real question.

286
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,950
Can I ask you one thing.

287
00:15:07,570 --> 00:15:08,930
He said, ask it.

288
00:15:09,630 --> 00:15:11,730
I had practiced a whole speech.

289
00:15:12,150 --> 00:15:15,270
The man got a lot of throat and the word so.

290
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:18,420
One question is a complete ask.

291
00:15:19,550 --> 00:15:22,370
What did you quit that kept your house in one piece.

292
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:25,280
How did you know a good offer was the wrong one.

293
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:29,250
Or can I work beside you and mostly keep quiet.

294
00:15:29,850 --> 00:15:32,750
If the man ahead says come by, you go.

295
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:35,240
If he says call, you call.

296
00:15:36,410 --> 00:15:40,360
Maybe you have a man that far ahead you've never really asked.

297
00:15:40,870 --> 00:15:43,550
That man is closer than the excuse.

298
00:15:44,570 --> 00:15:48,400
Once that man answers, bring a real question when you come again.

299
00:15:48,950 --> 00:15:50,790
The question is the honor.

300
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:54,160
If you only show up to hang around, he will drift.

301
00:15:54,650 --> 00:15:58,360
A man his age has had younger men nod and change nothing.

302
00:15:58,950 --> 00:16:01,590
Do the thing he said, at least once.

303
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,810
Then go back and tell him what happened.

304
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:06,780
That report is what earns the next talk.

305
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:10,120
Don't make the man ahead your father.

306
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:12,100
He can give you a great deal.

307
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:15,620
He can't fill the particular hole your father left.

308
00:16:16,090 --> 00:16:17,500
Thank him out loud.

309
00:16:17,990 --> 00:16:21,110
I did what you said about supper, and I stayed in the room.

310
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,090
Or maybe you're the older man.

311
00:16:24,570 --> 00:16:25,510
You're unfinished.

312
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:27,320
Nobody graduates.

313
00:16:27,750 --> 00:16:31,210
A younger man is walking into country you already crossed.

314
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:33,410
He doesn't need your clean record.

315
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:36,310
He needs the truth about where you failed,

316
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:39,920
and the ordinary things you kept that held the house anyway.

317
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:43,970
Titus two, verses six and seven.

318
00:16:44,610 --> 00:16:48,670
"Similarly, encourage the young men to be self-controlled.

319
00:16:49,290 --> 00:16:53,060
In everything set them an example by doing what is good."

320
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:56,870
A younger man won't start the ask.

321
00:16:57,320 --> 00:17:00,240
You make him nervous, and he has decided you're busy.

322
00:17:00,950 --> 00:17:02,720
Give him a yes he can take.

323
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:04,550
I'm replacing a faucet.

324
00:17:05,090 --> 00:17:08,700
Come hold the light if you want to see how an old man learns patience.

325
00:17:09,190 --> 00:17:10,820
Then skip the lecture.

326
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,170
Ask him what the work is doing to him.

327
00:17:13,730 --> 00:17:14,760
How it is at home.

328
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:15,930
What's heavy.

329
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,700
Leave him a little quiet after you ask.

330
00:17:19,910 --> 00:17:22,670
A younger man asked me if I had wisdom for him.

331
00:17:23,270 --> 00:17:24,920
I told him, give me a second.

332
00:17:25,450 --> 00:17:27,270
That second is still open.

333
00:17:27,690 --> 00:17:29,510
He didn't need my highlight reel.

334
00:17:29,930 --> 00:17:32,580
The highlight reel is how a man hides.

335
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:37,620
I missed a pile of ordinary nights and called the missing a season.

336
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:40,640
His shoulders dropped when I quit performing.

337
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:43,620
Your miss is often the useful part.

338
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:47,320
Another man, I'll call him Mack.

339
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:53,640
Mack had been the older face among the men so long he figured his record had retired him.

340
00:17:54,430 --> 00:17:55,420
Mack was kind.

341
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:57,740
Mack was done offering.

342
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:04,530
A younger man, new around there, asked Mack what the hard years at home had cost.

343
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:06,900
Mack almost waved him off.

344
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,880
Mack had the wave ready.

345
00:18:09,710 --> 00:18:11,850
Then Mack told the truth.

346
00:18:12,530 --> 00:18:17,050
Mack said he had given his best hours to the job and called it love,

347
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:19,530
and the house got what was left.

348
00:18:20,130 --> 00:18:21,200
Mack didn't dress it.

349
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:25,370
The young man came back after a stretch of days.

350
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:28,470
The young man said he had left his phone in the

351
00:18:28,470 --> 00:18:31,090
other room for supper and stayed inside the talk.

352
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:33,000
That was the whole assignment.

353
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:37,240
Mack told me afterward that he thought he was the one giving.

354
00:18:37,860 --> 00:18:41,920
Mostly that young man was keeping Mack awake to his own life.

355
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:47,330
If your mornings have gotten quiet, this is a worthy way to spend them.

356
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:52,510
God keeps putting men near each other and then waiting to see who will speak.

357
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:54,400
You can be the one.

358
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:58,400
Look twenty years up the road.

359
00:18:58,850 --> 00:19:01,470
Living those four marks most of the time.

360
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:06,440
You need a man still standing at the far end of a road like yours.

361
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:09,180
Watch whether he tells on himself.

362
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:13,440
A man with only wins can't take you where you need to go.

363
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,530
You came for the scar and for the habit he kept anyway.

364
00:19:18,110 --> 00:19:20,840
If no name comes, you're looking too high.

365
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:25,400
That man may be the one people thank and nobody asks.

366
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,550
Your silence has been part of his life too.

367
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:30,610
Maybe you're young.

368
00:19:31,110 --> 00:19:32,210
Awkward is allowed.

369
00:19:32,770 --> 00:19:33,610
You're not late.

370
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:34,910
Say it anyway.

371
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:39,880
Waiting until you feel smooth is how a boy stays a boy with a paycheck.

372
00:19:41,070 --> 00:19:42,430
Or maybe you're single.

373
00:19:42,910 --> 00:19:45,080
Don't store the ask until a wedding.

374
00:19:45,650 --> 00:19:48,000
The life you have needs a brother in it.

375
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:52,310
Ask a married man how a house is kept, before you have one.

376
00:19:52,850 --> 00:19:57,430
The men you share a roof with can be good company and still not know you.

377
00:19:58,040 --> 00:19:59,260
Add the one man.

378
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:01,800
Or maybe you're married.

379
00:20:02,350 --> 00:20:03,840
Tell your wife you asked.

380
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:07,120
Don't hand her the job of being the wise man.

381
00:20:07,650 --> 00:20:08,980
She is your wife.

382
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:14,160
If the marriage ended, shame is going to tell you to sit this out.

383
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:16,030
Ask anyway.

384
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:19,550
Go to a man who has walked through a marriage ending,

385
00:20:19,890 --> 00:20:23,210
or a long-married man who won't put you on display.

386
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:26,380
If you've been burned, hear me.

387
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,810
Asking isn't groveling.

388
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:32,500
Asking is courage, not a loss of dignity.

389
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:34,870
Or maybe you're older.

390
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:36,570
Be easy to stop.

391
00:20:37,180 --> 00:20:40,220
A younger man is already talking himself out of you.

392
00:20:40,810 --> 00:20:44,220
Go toward him and give him something he can say yes to.

393
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:46,580
Or maybe you're in the middle.

394
00:20:47,090 --> 00:20:50,670
A man ahead you've never asked about a house that got quiet.

395
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:55,180
A younger man behind you you've watched and never spoken to.

396
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:58,270
The chain needs you looking both ways.

397
00:20:59,330 --> 00:21:01,240
Or maybe the work has been strong.

398
00:21:01,770 --> 00:21:03,980
Ask a man who doesn't report to you.

399
00:21:04,510 --> 00:21:07,270
A full day can still leave you unknown.

400
00:21:08,530 --> 00:21:12,910
And if the season is tight, a short clear ask still counts.

401
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:15,920
A text that names a day and a time.

402
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:18,060
A sentence in a doorway.

403
00:21:18,730 --> 00:21:20,480
A hint isn't an ask.

404
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:22,680
Say the actual sentence.

405
00:21:23,070 --> 00:21:24,870
Set the time before you hang up.

406
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:30,220
You were not built to go down alone and call it strength.

407
00:21:30,890 --> 00:21:36,250
One man, one question, one honest answer, and keep coming back.

408
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:39,010
I hope you're done waiting to be picked.

409
00:21:39,530 --> 00:21:42,720
The awkward feeling means you found the right sentence.

410
00:21:43,830 --> 00:21:45,970
Turn to Lesson Twelve in the workbook.

411
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:47,830
Speak your answers.

412
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:49,200
First.

413
00:21:49,810 --> 00:21:53,530
If I fell, the man I could call is blank.

414
00:21:54,870 --> 00:21:57,300
Say the blank, or say the name.

415
00:21:57,910 --> 00:21:59,860
Your wife doesn't fill the blank.

416
00:22:00,510 --> 00:22:01,100
Second.

417
00:22:01,710 --> 00:22:04,980
Who is the man twenty years ahead you've never asked,

418
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:08,440
or the young man you've watched and never spoken to.

419
00:22:09,770 --> 00:22:10,250
Third.

420
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:14,830
What is the brother sentence, and what is the one real question.

421
00:22:16,380 --> 00:22:17,710
The sentence is plain.

422
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:21,670
I'm trying to be a better man, and I don't have a brother.

423
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:25,600
Would you sit with me, and keep at it, until it's real?

424
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:29,630
Set the day and the time before you put the phone down.

425
00:22:30,270 --> 00:22:32,540
One real question for the man ahead.

426
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:34,050
Write the question.

427
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:37,330
If you're older, write the yes you'll offer.

428
00:22:37,810 --> 00:22:41,060
A breakfast, a job beside you, or a call.

429
00:22:41,670 --> 00:22:43,400
Put the blank on the page.

430
00:22:43,810 --> 00:22:45,520
Put the ask on the page.

431
00:22:45,990 --> 00:22:48,900
A hint stays a hint until a man hears it.

432
00:22:50,090 --> 00:22:52,680
So here's your one move. One.

433
00:22:53,170 --> 00:22:57,490
Say the brother sentence to one man, or say that no name is ready,

434
00:22:57,890 --> 00:23:01,110
and set the day and the time before you put the phone down.

435
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:08,500
A steadfast man ends the wait, takes up what is his to carry, moves before he is called,

436
00:23:08,780 --> 00:23:13,510
and receives God's pay, while a crowd's approval stays out of the wage.

437
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:17,300
From this lesson on, that means you go first.

438
00:23:18,410 --> 00:23:21,300
Next lesson we look at the problem inside a man.

439
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:23,210
The Problem Inside.

440
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:24,930
Go say the sentence.

